    is not shipped with this repository, because it is real-environment data
    rather than project source. Users who need to reproduce the fact-checking
    paths that depend on it must capture their own snapshot from their own
    environment; the tooling fails closed when the snapshot is missing instead of
    silently substituting an empty one.

(c) `async_gaussdb` — optional extra, bring your own driver.

    The GaussDB collection path imports `async_gaussdb`, a non-public PyPI driver
    that is not distributed with this repository and is not available as a
    public package under that name. It is documented as an optional extra in
    `pyproject.toml`, and it intentionally has no wheel to install. Users who
    want to exercise the GaussDB collection path must supply their own
    interface-compatible implementation that is importable under the module name
    `async_gaussdb`, together with their own database credentials. Rationale: the
    driver is not the project's to redistribute. When it is not supplied, the
    affected collection and gate paths report BLOCKED by design.

(d) Neo4j, Ontotext GraphDB and Dify — separate third-party works, used as
