CONVENTIONS USED IN THIS REPOSITORY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(f) Placeholder paths and hosts in comments, defaults and sample output.

    This repository was extracted from a private working environment. Absolute
    paths, host names and addresses that belonged to that environment have been
    replaced by placeholders, and the substitution is intentional and
    consistent:

      * `<workspace>`, `<repo>`, `<upstream-repo>` — local working paths. The
        `upstream-ops-agent` workspace they refer to is the separate repository
        of the same author in which the collect layer described in (a) was
        originally developed; that tree is now part of this repository.
      * `/opt/upstream-agent`, `/opt/cc-ops` — example installation directories
        for the older `upstream-ops-agent` deployment and for a deployment of
        this project. They are defaults in shell scripts and Dockerfiles;
        override them for your own hosts.
      * `192.0.2.0/24` — RFC 5737 documentation addresses, used wherever real
        addresses appeared. They are not routable and not a deployment target.
      * `example.com` / `git.example.com` — example endpoints in the same spirit.

    Sample evidence, gate output and rationale strings therefore quote
    measurements taken on hardware that is not yours. They are kept verbatim
    because they are the justification for declared thresholds; treat them as
    historical records, not as values that must hold in your environment.
